IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `euca-nouns`
IMPORT `euca-shared`
IMPORT `euca-s203-period`
IMPORT `euca-s202-work-test`
IMPORT `euca-s202-conditions`
IMPORT `euca-s202-account`
IMPORT `euca-s202-payable`

-- Tests for section 202(a): who extended compensation is payable to, week by week.
-- Every expected value was worked out by hand from the text before the file was run, and each
-- case says what the hand calculation was. Nothing here is a rule of the Act.
-- Money is in dollars; weeks are dates on which a week begins.

§ `Tests: section 202(a), who extended compensation is payable to`

§§ `Fixtures`

GIVEN received IS A BOOLEAN
      stateRights IS A BOOLEAN
      otherStateRights IS A BOOLEAN
      otherFederal IS A BOOLEAN
      canada IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Regular compensation position`
`in the eligibility tests, a position of` received stateRights otherStateRights otherFederal canada MEANS
    `Regular compensation position` WITH
        `received all the regular compensation available on the base period employment or wages` IS received
        `rights to regular compensation for the week under the State law` IS stateRights
        `rights to regular compensation for the week under another State's unemployment compensation law` IS otherStateRights
        `compensation for the week under another Federal law` IS otherFederal
        `receiving compensation for the week under the unemployment compensation law of Canada` IS canada

GIVEN how IS A `How the work reached the individual`
      accepted IS A BOOLEAN
      applied IS A BOOLEAN
      within IS A BOOLEAN
      good IS A BOOLEAN
      stateSuitable IS A BOOLEAN
      remuneration IS A NUMBER
      supplemental IS A NUMBER
      inWriting IS A BOOLEAN
      listed IS A BOOLEAN
      wouldDeny IS A BOOLEAN
      wage IS A NUMBER
      stateMinimum IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `Offer of work or referral`
`in the eligibility tests, an offer of` how accepted applied within good stateSuitable remuneration supplemental inWriting listed wouldDeny wage stateMinimum MEANS
    `Offer of work or referral` WITH
        `how the work reached the individual` IS how
        `the individual accepted the offer` IS accepted
        `the individual applied for the work to which the State agency referred them` IS applied
        `the work is within the individual's capabilities` IS within
        `the individual furnished evidence satisfactory to the State agency that prospects of work in the customary occupation are good` IS good
        `the applicable State law treats the work as suitable` IS stateSuitable
        `gross average weekly remuneration payable for the position` IS remuneration
        `average weekly benefit amount for the individual's benefit year` IS 400
        `supplemental unemployment compensation benefits payable to the individual for the week` IS supplemental
        `the position was offered to the individual in writing` IS inWriting
        `the position was listed with the State employment service` IS listed
        `State law, so far as consistent with C and E, would deny compensation for the failure` IS wouldDeny
        `wages the position pays per hour` IS wage
        `Fair Labor Standards Act section 6(a)(1) minimum wage per hour, without regard to any exemption` IS 7.25
        `highest applicable State or local minimum wage per hour, or 0 if there is none` IS stateMinimum

-- A job that was offered, is within the individual's capabilities, pays 500 a week against a benefit of 400,
-- was offered in writing, would be penalised by State law, and pays 10 an hour: refusing it is a denial.
`in the eligibility tests, a plainly refused offer` MEANS
    `in the eligibility tests, an offer of` `offered to the individual` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE 500 0 TRUE FALSE TRUE 10 0

GIVEN effort IS A BOOLEAN
      evidence IS A BOOLEAN
      jury IS A BOOLEAN
      juryRegular IS A BOOLEAN
      juryExtended IS A BOOLEAN
      hospital IS A BOOLEAN
      hospitalRegular IS A BOOLEAN
      hospitalExtended IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Search for work`
`in the eligibility tests, a search of` effort evidence jury juryRegular juryExtended hospital hospitalRegular hospitalExtended MEANS
    `Search for work` WITH
        `engaged in a systematic and sustained effort to obtain work during the week` IS effort
        `provided tangible evidence to the State agency of that effort` IS evidence
        `before a court of the United States or of a State pursuant to a lawfully issued summons to appear for jury duty` IS jury
        `hospitalized for treatment of an emergency or a life-threatening condition` IS hospital
        `the jury duty exemption applies to recipients of regular benefits` IS juryRegular
        `the State chooses to apply the jury duty exemption to recipients of extended benefits` IS juryExtended
        `the hospitalization exemption applies to recipients of regular benefits` IS hospitalRegular
        `the State chooses to apply the hospitalization exemption to recipients of extended benefits` IS hospitalExtended

GIVEN failedWeek IS A MAYBE DATE
      weeks IS A NUMBER
      remuneration IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `Earlier failure`
`in the eligibility tests, an earlier failure of` failedWeek weeks remuneration MEANS
    `Earlier failure` WITH
        `week in which the failure occurred, if there was one` IS failedWeek
        `weeks of employment that began after the failure and before the week claimed` IS weeks
        `remuneration earned for being so employed` IS remuneration
        `average weekly benefit amount for the individual's benefit year` IS 400

GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of disqualification`
      terminated IS A BOOLEAN
      onSubsequentEmployment IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Disqualification
`in the eligibility tests, a disqualification of` kind terminated onSubsequentEmployment MEANS
    Disqualification WITH
        `kind of disqualification` IS kind
        `the State law has terminated the disqualification` IS terminated
        `the termination is based upon employment subsequent to the date of the disqualification` IS onSubsequentEmployment

GIVEN weeks IS A NUMBER
      earnings IS A NUMBER
      weeklyAmount IS A NUMBER
      quarter IS A NUMBER
      method20 IS A BOOLEAN
      method40 IS A BOOLEAN
      methodHalf IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Employment in the base period`
`in the eligibility tests, employment of` weeks earnings weeklyAmount quarter method20 method40 methodHalf MEANS
    `Employment in the base period` WITH
        `weeks of full-time insured employment in the base period` IS weeks
        `earnings covered by the State law in the base period` IS earnings
        `most recent weekly benefit amount` IS weeklyAmount
        `insured wages in the calendar quarter of the base period in which they were highest` IS quarter
        `the State law uses the 20 weeks of full-time insured employment method` IS method20
        `the State law uses the earnings above 40 times the weekly benefit amount method` IS method40
        `the State law uses the earnings above one and a half times the highest quarter method` IS methodHalf

GIVEN wouldBePayable IS A BOOLEAN
      ebpInClaimState IS A BOOLEAN
      earlierWeeks IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `Interstate claim`
`in the eligibility tests, an interstate claim of` wouldBePayable ebpInClaimState earlierWeeks MEANS
    `Interstate claim` WITH
        `extended compensation would but for the cessation rule have been payable for the week pursuant to an interstate claim under the interstate benefit payment plan` IS wouldBePayable
        `an extended benefit period is in effect for the week in the State where the claim was filed` IS ebpInClaimState
        `earlier weeks for which extended compensation was payable pursuant to the interstate claim from the account` IS earlierWeeks

-- A benefit year of 4 March 2012 to 3 March 2013, and one of 1 March 2012 to 28 February 2013.
`in the eligibility tests, a benefit year ending 3 March 2013` MEANS
    `Benefit year` WITH
        `first day of the benefit year` IS Date 4 3 2012
        `last day of the benefit year` IS Date 3 3 2013

`in the eligibility tests, a benefit year ending 28 February 2013` MEANS
    `Benefit year` WITH
        `first day of the benefit year` IS Date 1 3 2012
        `last day of the benefit year` IS Date 28 2 2013

`in the eligibility tests, the period of 3 February to 28 April 2013` MEANS
    `Extended benefit period` WITH
        `first week of the extended benefit period` IS Date 3 2 2013
        `last week of the extended benefit period` IS JUST (Date 28 4 2013)

-- Regular compensation payable in the benefit year 10,000, weekly benefit amount 400, regular compensation paid 10,000.
-- Section 202(b)(1): (A) 50 per cent of 10,000 is 5,000; (B) 13 x 400 is 5,200; (C) 39 x 400 less 10,000 is 5,600. Least: 5,000.
`in the eligibility tests, an ordinary account` MEANS
    `Account facts` WITH
        `total regular compensation payable during the benefit year, including dependents' allowances` IS 10000
        `average weekly benefit amount` IS 400
        `regular compensation paid or deemed paid during the benefit year` IS 10000
        `the State law reduces the account by additional compensation paid` IS FALSE
        `additional compensation paid or deemed paid for prior weeks in the benefit year that did not begin in an extended benefit period` IS 0
        `the week begins in a high unemployment period` IS FALSE

`in the eligibility tests, an ordinary interstate claim` MEANS
    `in the eligibility tests, an interstate claim of` FALSE FALSE 0

`in the eligibility tests, employment meeting the 20 weeks method` MEANS
    `in the eligibility tests, employment of` 52 20000 300 6000 TRUE FALSE FALSE

`in the eligibility tests, no failure` MEANS
    `in the eligibility tests, an earlier failure of` NOTHING 0 0

`in the eligibility tests, a search that satisfies subparagraph E` MEANS
    `in the eligibility tests, a search of` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE

§§ `202(a)(1): exhaustion`

-- The benefit year ends 3 March 2013. A week beginning on the last day is in the benefit year: not expired.
#ASSERT NOT (`the individual has exhausted all rights to regular compensation` (Date 3 3 2013) (`in the eligibility tests, a benefit year ending 3 March 2013`) (`in the eligibility tests, a position of` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE))
-- A week beginning the day after the last day: the rights terminated "by reason of the expiration of the benefit year" ((B)).
#ASSERT `the individual has exhausted all rights to regular compensation` (Date 4 3 2013) (`in the eligibility tests, a benefit year ending 3 March 2013`) (`in the eligibility tests, a position of` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- (A): all the regular compensation available has been received, whatever the date.
#ASSERT `the individual has exhausted all rights to regular compensation` (Date 3 3 2013) (`in the eligibility tests, a benefit year ending 3 March 2013`) (`in the eligibility tests, a position of` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)

§§ `202(a)(1): no other rights for the week`

#ASSERT `the individual has no other rights to compensation for the week` (`in the eligibility tests, a position of` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the individual has no other rights to compensation for the week` (`in the eligibility tests, a position of` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`the individual has no other rights to compensation for the week` (`in the eligibility tests, a position of` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`the individual has no other rights to compensation for the week` (`in the eligibility tests, a position of` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`the individual has no other rights to compensation for the week` (`in the eligibility tests, a position of` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE))

§§ `202(a)(1): the State law must provide payment`

#ASSERT `the State law must provide payment of extended compensation for the week` (Date 24 2 2013) (`in the eligibility tests, a benefit year ending 28 February 2013`) (`in the eligibility tests, a position of` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) TRUE
-- A week outside the eligibility period.
#ASSERT NOT (`the State law must provide payment of extended compensation for the week` (Date 24 2 2013) (`in the eligibility tests, a benefit year ending 28 February 2013`) (`in the eligibility tests, a position of` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) FALSE)
-- Regular compensation not yet exhausted (week 24 February, benefit year runs to 28 February, some regular compensation still available).
#ASSERT NOT (`the State law must provide payment of extended compensation for the week` (Date 24 2 2013) (`in the eligibility tests, a benefit year ending 28 February 2013`) (`in the eligibility tests, a position of` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) TRUE)
-- Rights to regular compensation for the week under the State law.
#ASSERT NOT (`the State law must provide payment of extended compensation for the week` (Date 24 2 2013) (`in the eligibility tests, a benefit year ending 28 February 2013`) (`in the eligibility tests, a position of` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) TRUE)

§§ `202(a)(2): the State law's terms for regular claims`

#ASSERT `a State rule for regular compensation claims applies to extended compensation claims` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`a State rule for regular compensation claims applies to extended compensation claims` TRUE)

§§ `202(a)(3)(C): suitable work`

-- Within the individual's capabilities, no evidence of good prospects: suitable.
#ASSERT `the work is suitable work` (`in the eligibility tests, an offer of` `offered to the individual` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE 500 0 TRUE FALSE TRUE 10 0)
-- Not within capabilities: not suitable.
#ASSERT NOT (`the work is suitable work` (`in the eligibility tests, an offer of` `offered to the individual` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 500 0 TRUE FALSE TRUE 10 0))
-- Evidence of good prospects: State law decides. Within capabilities but State law says no: not suitable.
#ASSERT NOT (`the work is suitable work` (`in the eligibility tests, an offer of` `offered to the individual` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE 500 0 TRUE FALSE TRUE 10 0))
-- Evidence of good prospects, not within capabilities, State law says suitable: suitable.
#ASSERT `the work is suitable work` (`in the eligibility tests, an offer of` `offered to the individual` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE 500 0 TRUE FALSE TRUE 10 0)

§§ `202(a)(3)(A)(i): refusing an offer, or not applying for referred work`

#ASSERT `extended compensation is denied under clause (i) for the offer or referral` (`in the eligibility tests, a plainly refused offer`)
-- Accepted: no failure.
#ASSERT NOT (`extended compensation is denied under clause (i) for the offer or referral` (`in the eligibility tests, an offer of` `offered to the individual` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE 500 0 TRUE FALSE TRUE 10 0))
-- Referred, not applied: failure. Referred and applied: none. (Accepting a referral is not the question; applying is.)
#ASSERT `extended compensation is denied under clause (i) for the offer or referral` (`in the eligibility tests, an offer of` `referred to the individual by the State agency` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE 500 0 TRUE FALSE TRUE 10 0)
#ASSERT NOT (`extended compensation is denied under clause (i) for the offer or referral` (`in the eligibility tests, an offer of` `referred to the individual by the State agency` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 500 0 TRUE FALSE TRUE 10 0))
-- A referral is not "accepted" by accepting it: applying is the step. An offer is not "applied for".
#ASSERT `extended compensation is denied under clause (i) for the offer or referral` (`in the eligibility tests, an offer of` `referred to the individual by the State agency` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE 500 0 TRUE FALSE TRUE 10 0)
#ASSERT `extended compensation is denied under clause (i) for the offer or referral` (`in the eligibility tests, an offer of` `offered to the individual` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 500 0 TRUE FALSE TRUE 10 0)
-- Unsuitable work refused: no denial.
#ASSERT NOT (`extended compensation is denied under clause (i) for the offer or referral` (`in the eligibility tests, an offer of` `offered to the individual` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 500 0 TRUE FALSE TRUE 10 0))

§§ `202(a)(3)(D): offers that may be turned down`

-- (i): pay 400 against a weekly benefit amount of 400 and no supplemental benefits: "does not exceed": exception applies.
#ASSERT NOT (`extended compensation is denied under clause (i) for the offer or referral` (`in the eligibility tests, an offer of` `offered to the individual` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE 400 0 TRUE FALSE TRUE 10 0))
-- (i): pay 401 exceeds 400: refusing it is a denial.
#ASSERT `extended compensation is denied under clause (i) for the offer or referral` (`in the eligibility tests, an offer of` `offered to the individual` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE 401 0 TRUE FALSE TRUE 10 0)
-- (i): with 50 of supplemental unemployment compensation benefits the threshold is 450.
#ASSERT NOT (`extended compensation is denied under clause (i) for the offer or referral` (`in the eligibility tests, an offer of` `offered to the individual` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE 450 50 TRUE FALSE TRUE 10 0))
#ASSERT `extended compensation is denied under clause (i) for the offer or referral` (`in the eligibility tests, an offer of` `offered to the individual` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE 451 50 TRUE FALSE TRUE 10 0)
-- (ii): neither offered in writing nor listed: exception applies.
#ASSERT NOT (`extended compensation is denied under clause (i) for the offer or referral` (`in the eligibility tests, an offer of` `offered to the individual` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE 500 0 FALSE FALSE TRUE 10 0))
-- (ii): listed but not in writing: no exception from (ii).
#ASSERT `extended compensation is denied under clause (i) for the offer or referral` (`in the eligibility tests, an offer of` `offered to the individual` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE 500 0 FALSE TRUE TRUE 10 0)
-- (iii): State law would not deny: exception applies.
#ASSERT NOT (`extended compensation is denied under clause (i) for the offer or referral` (`in the eligibility tests, an offer of` `offered to the individual` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE 500 0 TRUE FALSE FALSE 10 0))
-- (iv): 7.00 an hour is below the federal minimum 7.25: exception applies. 7.25 is not less than 7.25: no exception.
#ASSERT NOT (`extended compensation is denied under clause (i) for the offer or referral` (`in the eligibility tests, an offer of` `offered to the individual` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE 500 0 TRUE FALSE TRUE 7 0))
#ASSERT `extended compensation is denied under clause (i) for the offer or referral` (`in the eligibility tests, an offer of` `offered to the individual` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE 500 0 TRUE FALSE TRUE 7.25 0)
-- (iv): the higher of the federal 7.25 and a State minimum of 8: 7.5 is below 8, 8 is not.
#ASSERT NOT (`extended compensation is denied under clause (i) for the offer or referral` (`in the eligibility tests, an offer of` `offered to the individual` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE 500 0 TRUE FALSE TRUE 7.5 8))
#ASSERT `extended compensation is denied under clause (i) for the offer or referral` (`in the eligibility tests, an offer of` `offered to the individual` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE 500 0 TRUE FALSE TRUE 8 8)
-- (F): the State law must refer applicants to suitable work to which none of (i) to (iv) applies; the plain offer is one.
#ASSERT `the State law must provide for referring applicants to the work` (`in the eligibility tests, a plainly refused offer`)
#ASSERT NOT (`the State law must provide for referring applicants to the work` (`in the eligibility tests, an offer of` `offered to the individual` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE 400 0 TRUE FALSE TRUE 10 0))
#ASSERT NOT (`the State law must provide for referring applicants to the work` (`in the eligibility tests, an offer of` `offered to the individual` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 500 0 TRUE FALSE TRUE 10 0))
-- Any one offer among several is enough; none is no denial.
#ASSERT `extended compensation is denied under clause (i) for any offer or referral` (LIST (`in the eligibility tests, an offer of` `offered to the individual` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE 500 0 TRUE FALSE TRUE 10 0), (`in the eligibility tests, a plainly refused offer`))
#ASSERT NOT (`extended compensation is denied under clause (i) for any offer or referral` (LIST (`in the eligibility tests, an offer of` `offered to the individual` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE 500 0 TRUE FALSE TRUE 10 0)))
#ASSERT NOT (`extended compensation is denied under clause (i) for any offer or referral` (EMPTY))

§§ `202(a)(3)(A)(ii) and (E): seeking work`

#ASSERT `the individual is treated as actively engaged in seeking work` (`in the eligibility tests, a search of` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- Effort without tangible evidence is not enough, and nor is evidence without effort ((E) needs both).
#ASSERT NOT (`the individual is treated as actively engaged in seeking work` (`in the eligibility tests, a search of` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`the individual is treated as actively engaged in seeking work` (`in the eligibility tests, a search of` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`extended compensation is denied under clause (ii) for failing to seek work` (`in the eligibility tests, a search that satisfies subparagraph E`))
#ASSERT `extended compensation is denied under clause (ii) for failing to seek work` (`in the eligibility tests, a search of` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- Jury duty: needs the summons, the exemption for regular benefits AND the State's choice for extended benefits.
#ASSERT NOT (`extended compensation is denied under clause (ii) for failing to seek work` (`in the eligibility tests, a search of` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE))
#ASSERT `extended compensation is denied under clause (ii) for failing to seek work` (`in the eligibility tests, a search of` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `extended compensation is denied under clause (ii) for failing to seek work` (`in the eligibility tests, a search of` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `extended compensation is denied under clause (ii) for failing to seek work` (`in the eligibility tests, a search of` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- Hospitalised for an emergency: the same three conditions.
#ASSERT NOT (`extended compensation is denied under clause (ii) for failing to seek work` (`in the eligibility tests, a search of` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE))
#ASSERT `extended compensation is denied under clause (ii) for failing to seek work` (`in the eligibility tests, a search of` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- The jury exemption does not borrow the hospital exemption's State choice.
#ASSERT `extended compensation is denied under clause (ii) for failing to seek work` (`in the eligibility tests, a search of` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE)

§§ `202(a)(3)(B): how long the ineligibility lasts`

-- A failure in the week of 3 February 2013; average weekly benefit amount 400: 4 weeks of work and 1,600 end it.
#ASSERT NOT (`the period of ineligibility after an earlier failure has ended` (`in the eligibility tests, an earlier failure of` (JUST (Date 3 2 2013)) 3 5000))
#ASSERT NOT (`the period of ineligibility after an earlier failure has ended` (`in the eligibility tests, an earlier failure of` (JUST (Date 3 2 2013)) 4 1599))
#ASSERT `the period of ineligibility after an earlier failure has ended` (`in the eligibility tests, an earlier failure of` (JUST (Date 3 2 2013)) 4 1600)
#ASSERT `the period of ineligibility after an earlier failure has ended` (`in the eligibility tests, an earlier failure of` (JUST (Date 3 2 2013)) 6 2400)
-- The week after the failure (10 February) is the first week of the ineligibility; the failure week itself is not "a week which begins" in it.
#ASSERT `the week begins during the period of ineligibility after an earlier failure` (Date 10 2 2013) (`in the eligibility tests, an earlier failure of` (JUST (Date 3 2 2013)) 0 0)
#ASSERT NOT (`the week begins during the period of ineligibility after an earlier failure` (Date 3 2 2013) (`in the eligibility tests, an earlier failure of` (JUST (Date 3 2 2013)) 0 0))
-- Once the work is done the ineligibility is over.
#ASSERT NOT (`the week begins during the period of ineligibility after an earlier failure` (Date 17 3 2013) (`in the eligibility tests, an earlier failure of` (JUST (Date 3 2 2013)) 4 1600))
-- No failure at all: never ineligible.
#ASSERT NOT (`the week begins during the period of ineligibility after an earlier failure` (Date 17 3 2013) (`in the eligibility tests, no failure`))
-- What is still needed: 3 weeks worked means 1 more; 5 weeks means none; 1,000 earned means 600 more; 2,000 means none.
#ASSERT `weeks of employment still needed to end the period of ineligibility` (`in the eligibility tests, an earlier failure of` (JUST (Date 3 2 2013)) 3 1000) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `weeks of employment still needed to end the period of ineligibility` (`in the eligibility tests, an earlier failure of` (JUST (Date 3 2 2013)) 5 1000) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `remuneration still needed to end the period of ineligibility` (`in the eligibility tests, an earlier failure of` (JUST (Date 3 2 2013)) 3 1000) EQUALS 600
#ASSERT `remuneration still needed to end the period of ineligibility` (`in the eligibility tests, an earlier failure of` (JUST (Date 3 2 2013)) 5 2000) EQUALS 0

§§ `202(a)(3): the work test as a whole`

-- A refused offer bars the week.
#ASSERT `the work test bars extended compensation for the week` (Date 24 2 2013) (LIST (`in the eligibility tests, a plainly refused offer`)) (`in the eligibility tests, a search that satisfies subparagraph E`) (`in the eligibility tests, no failure`)
-- Not seeking work bars the week.
#ASSERT `the work test bars extended compensation for the week` (Date 24 2 2013) (EMPTY) (`in the eligibility tests, a search of` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) (`in the eligibility tests, no failure`)
-- A failure not yet cured bars the week although this week's search is fine.
#ASSERT `the work test bars extended compensation for the week` (Date 24 2 2013) (EMPTY) (`in the eligibility tests, a search that satisfies subparagraph E`) (`in the eligibility tests, an earlier failure of` (JUST (Date 3 2 2013)) 2 800)
-- None of the three: not barred.
#ASSERT NOT (`the work test bars extended compensation for the week` (Date 24 2 2013) (EMPTY) (`in the eligibility tests, a search that satisfies subparagraph E`) (`in the eligibility tests, no failure`))

§§ `202(a)(4): disqualifications the State law would end`

-- The State law has terminated the disqualification, but not because of later employment: it still bars.
#ASSERT `the disqualification still bars extended compensation` (`in the eligibility tests, a disqualification of` `voluntarily leaving employment` TRUE FALSE)
-- Terminated because of employment after the disqualification: the termination counts.
#ASSERT NOT (`the disqualification still bars extended compensation` (`in the eligibility tests, a disqualification of` `being discharged for misconduct` TRUE TRUE))
-- Not terminated: still bars.
#ASSERT `the disqualification still bars extended compensation` (`in the eligibility tests, a disqualification of` `refusing suitable employment` FALSE FALSE)
-- One of several is enough; no disqualification, none bars.
#ASSERT `a disqualification still bars extended compensation` (LIST (`in the eligibility tests, a disqualification of` `being discharged for misconduct` TRUE TRUE), (`in the eligibility tests, a disqualification of` `refusing suitable employment` FALSE FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`a disqualification still bars extended compensation` (LIST (`in the eligibility tests, a disqualification of` `being discharged for misconduct` TRUE TRUE)))
#ASSERT NOT (`a disqualification still bars extended compensation` (EMPTY))

§§ `202(a)(5): the employment the individual must have had`

-- The State uses the 20-weeks method only. 20 weeks: has it; 19: lacks it, whatever the earnings.
#ASSERT `the result of the employment requirement` (`in the eligibility tests, employment of` 20 0 300 0 TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `the individual has the required employment`
#ASSERT `the result of the employment requirement` (`in the eligibility tests, employment of` 19 99999 300 1000 TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `the individual lacks the required employment`
-- The 40 x method only, weekly benefit amount 300: 40 x 300 = 12,000. Earnings must EXCEED: 12,000 lacks, 12,001 has.
#ASSERT `the result of the employment requirement` (`in the eligibility tests, employment of` 0 12000 300 0 FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS `the individual lacks the required employment`
#ASSERT `the result of the employment requirement` (`in the eligibility tests, employment of` 0 12001 300 0 FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS `the individual has the required employment`
-- The 1.5 x highest quarter method only: quarter 4,000, 1.5 x 4,000 = 6,000. 6,000 lacks, 6,001 has.
#ASSERT `the result of the employment requirement` (`in the eligibility tests, employment of` 0 6000 300 4000 FALSE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS `the individual lacks the required employment`
#ASSERT `the result of the employment requirement` (`in the eligibility tests, employment of` 0 6001 300 4000 FALSE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS `the individual has the required employment`
-- A method the State has not chosen does not help: only the 20-weeks method is used; 19 weeks with 99,999 earnings lacks (above).
-- Two methods chosen: meeting either is enough (19 weeks, but earnings of 12,001 over 40 x 300).
#ASSERT `the result of the employment requirement` (`in the eligibility tests, employment of` 19 12001 300 0 TRUE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS `the individual has the required employment`
-- No method chosen: the Act requires the State to choose; the individual's position is not decided by the Act.
#ASSERT `the result of the employment requirement` (`in the eligibility tests, employment of` 52 99999 300 4000 FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `the State law has chosen no method, which section 202(a)(5) requires it to do`

§§ `202(a)(7): when paragraphs (3) and (4) do not apply`

-- Not applied to weeks beginning after 6 March 1993 and before 1 January 1995.
#ASSERT `paragraphs (3) and (4) of section 202(a) apply to the week` (Date 6 3 1993)
#ASSERT NOT (`paragraphs (3) and (4) of section 202(a) apply to the week` (Date 7 3 1993))
#ASSERT NOT (`paragraphs (3) and (4) of section 202(a) apply to the week` (Date 31 12 1994))
#ASSERT `paragraphs (3) and (4) of section 202(a) apply to the week` (Date 1 1 1995)
#ASSERT `paragraphs (3) and (4) of section 202(a) apply to the week` (Date 24 2 2013)
-- In the suspended period a refused offer does not bar; the same facts bar in 2013.
#ASSERT NOT (`the work test bars extended compensation for the week unless section 202(a)(7) suspends it` (Date 1 6 1993) (LIST (`in the eligibility tests, a plainly refused offer`)) (`in the eligibility tests, a search that satisfies subparagraph E`) (`in the eligibility tests, no failure`))
#ASSERT `the work test bars extended compensation for the week unless section 202(a)(7) suspends it` (Date 1 6 2013) (LIST (`in the eligibility tests, a plainly refused offer`)) (`in the eligibility tests, a search that satisfies subparagraph E`) (`in the eligibility tests, no failure`)
-- The same for a disqualification not ended.
#ASSERT NOT (`a disqualification bars extended compensation for the week unless section 202(a)(7) suspends it` (Date 1 6 1993) (LIST (`in the eligibility tests, a disqualification of` `refusing suitable employment` FALSE FALSE)))
#ASSERT `a disqualification bars extended compensation for the week unless section 202(a)(7) suspends it` (Date 1 6 2013) (LIST (`in the eligibility tests, a disqualification of` `refusing suitable employment` FALSE FALSE))

§§ `202(a)(6): no payment to the State where paragraphs (3), (4) and (5) would not have allowed the payment`

-- A refused offer in 1990 (rules applied): no payment to the State. The same facts in the suspended period: payment.
#ASSERT `no payment is made to the State for the week under section 202(a)(6)` (Date 1 6 1990) TRUE FALSE `the individual has the required employment`
#ASSERT NOT (`no payment is made to the State for the week under section 202(a)(6)` (Date 1 6 1993) TRUE FALSE `the individual has the required employment`)
#ASSERT `no payment is made to the State for the week under section 202(a)(6)` (Date 1 6 1990) FALSE TRUE `the individual has the required employment`
#ASSERT NOT (`no payment is made to the State for the week under section 202(a)(6)` (Date 1 6 1993) FALSE TRUE `the individual has the required employment`)
-- Paragraph (5) is not suspended.
#ASSERT `no payment is made to the State for the week under section 202(a)(6)` (Date 1 6 1993) FALSE FALSE `the individual lacks the required employment`
#ASSERT `no payment is made to the State for the week under section 202(a)(6)` (Date 1 6 1993) FALSE FALSE `the State law has chosen no method, which section 202(a)(5) requires it to do`
-- Nothing bars and the employment is there: payment.
#ASSERT NOT (`no payment is made to the State for the week under section 202(a)(6)` (Date 1 6 1990) FALSE FALSE `the individual has the required employment`)

§§ `202(a), (b), (c) together: whether extended compensation is payable for the week`

GIVEN week IS A DATE
      position IS A `Regular compensation position`
      offers IS A LIST OF `Offer of work or referral`
      failure IS AN `Earlier failure`
      disqualifications IS A LIST OF Disqualification
      employment IS AN `Employment in the base period`
      interstate IS AN `Interstate claim`
      paid IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`in the eligibility tests, extended compensation is payable with` week position offers failure disqualifications employment interstate paid MEANS
    `extended compensation is payable for the week` week (`in the eligibility tests, a benefit year ending 28 February 2013`) (`in the eligibility tests, the period of 3 February to 28 April 2013`) position offers (`in the eligibility tests, a search that satisfies subparagraph E`) failure disqualifications employment interstate (`in the eligibility tests, an ordinary account`) paid

-- The ordinary case: in the period, exhausted, no other rights, nothing bars, 20 weeks of employment, nothing paid yet.
#ASSERT `in the eligibility tests, extended compensation is payable with` (Date 24 2 2013) (`in the eligibility tests, a position of` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) (EMPTY) (`in the eligibility tests, no failure`) (EMPTY) (`in the eligibility tests, employment meeting the 20 weeks method`) (`in the eligibility tests, an ordinary interstate claim`) 0
-- The account holds 5,000 (hand calculation above): 4,600 paid leaves room; 5,000 paid does not.
#ASSERT `in the eligibility tests, extended compensation is payable with` (Date 24 2 2013) (`in the eligibility tests, a position of` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) (EMPTY) (`in the eligibility tests, no failure`) (EMPTY) (`in the eligibility tests, employment meeting the 20 weeks method`) (`in the eligibility tests, an ordinary interstate claim`) 4600
#ASSERT NOT (`in the eligibility tests, extended compensation is payable with` (Date 24 2 2013) (`in the eligibility tests, a position of` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) (EMPTY) (`in the eligibility tests, no failure`) (EMPTY) (`in the eligibility tests, employment meeting the 20 weeks method`) (`in the eligibility tests, an ordinary interstate claim`) 5000)
-- Week outside the eligibility period (27 January 2013, before the period begins).
#ASSERT NOT (`in the eligibility tests, extended compensation is payable with` (Date 27 1 2013) (`in the eligibility tests, a position of` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) (EMPTY) (`in the eligibility tests, no failure`) (EMPTY) (`in the eligibility tests, employment meeting the 20 weeks method`) (`in the eligibility tests, an ordinary interstate claim`) 0)
-- Other rights to compensation for the week.
#ASSERT NOT (`in the eligibility tests, extended compensation is payable with` (Date 24 2 2013) (`in the eligibility tests, a position of` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE) (EMPTY) (`in the eligibility tests, no failure`) (EMPTY) (`in the eligibility tests, employment meeting the 20 weeks method`) (`in the eligibility tests, an ordinary interstate claim`) 0)
-- A refused offer.
#ASSERT NOT (`in the eligibility tests, extended compensation is payable with` (Date 24 2 2013) (`in the eligibility tests, a position of` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) (LIST (`in the eligibility tests, a plainly refused offer`)) (`in the eligibility tests, no failure`) (EMPTY) (`in the eligibility tests, employment meeting the 20 weeks method`) (`in the eligibility tests, an ordinary interstate claim`) 0)
-- A disqualification not ended.
#ASSERT NOT (`in the eligibility tests, extended compensation is payable with` (Date 24 2 2013) (`in the eligibility tests, a position of` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) (EMPTY) (`in the eligibility tests, no failure`) (LIST (`in the eligibility tests, a disqualification of` `voluntarily leaving employment` FALSE FALSE)) (`in the eligibility tests, employment meeting the 20 weeks method`) (`in the eligibility tests, an ordinary interstate claim`) 0)
-- Not enough employment in the base period (19 weeks under the 20-weeks method).
#ASSERT NOT (`in the eligibility tests, extended compensation is payable with` (Date 24 2 2013) (`in the eligibility tests, a position of` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) (EMPTY) (`in the eligibility tests, no failure`) (EMPTY) (`in the eligibility tests, employment of` 19 20000 300 6000 TRUE FALSE FALSE) (`in the eligibility tests, an ordinary interstate claim`) 0)
-- Interstate claim in a State with no extended benefit period, third week of payment: stopped by subsection (c).
#ASSERT NOT (`in the eligibility tests, extended compensation is payable with` (Date 24 2 2013) (`in the eligibility tests, a position of` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) (EMPTY) (`in the eligibility tests, no failure`) (EMPTY) (`in the eligibility tests, employment meeting the 20 weeks method`) (`in the eligibility tests, an interstate claim of` TRUE FALSE 2) 0)
-- Interstate claim, second week: the first 2 weeks are exempt, so the payment is made.
#ASSERT `in the eligibility tests, extended compensation is payable with` (Date 24 2 2013) (`in the eligibility tests, a position of` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) (EMPTY) (`in the eligibility tests, no failure`) (EMPTY) (`in the eligibility tests, employment meeting the 20 weeks method`) (`in the eligibility tests, an interstate claim of` TRUE FALSE 1) 0
-- The 3 March 2013 week: the benefit year ended 28 February 2013 but ends within the period, so the week counts, and the rights are exhausted by expiry.
#ASSERT `in the eligibility tests, extended compensation is payable with` (Date 3 3 2013) (`in the eligibility tests, a position of` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) (EMPTY) (`in the eligibility tests, no failure`) (EMPTY) (`in the eligibility tests, employment meeting the 20 weeks method`) (`in the eligibility tests, an ordinary interstate claim`) 0

-- Whether the State may be paid its share (202(a)(6)) for a week in which the individual should not have been paid.
#ASSERT `the State may not be paid its share of extended compensation paid for the week` (Date 24 2 2013) (LIST (`in the eligibility tests, a plainly refused offer`)) (`in the eligibility tests, a search that satisfies subparagraph E`) (`in the eligibility tests, no failure`) (EMPTY) (`in the eligibility tests, employment meeting the 20 weeks method`)
#ASSERT NOT (`the State may not be paid its share of extended compensation paid for the week` (Date 24 2 2013) (EMPTY) (`in the eligibility tests, a search that satisfies subparagraph E`) (`in the eligibility tests, no failure`) (EMPTY) (`in the eligibility tests, employment meeting the 20 weeks method`))
